    "reasoning": "Nitpicks: None that materially matter here (e.g., not providing a URL is fine since the task didn’t ask for it; choosing Madden NFL 27 vs another best-seller would be fine).\n\nCritical issues: The agent did not provide the publisher, which is one of the three explicitly required outputs and part of the stopping condition (“recording the publisher, developer, and release date”). Screenshots/DOM evidence (States 5 and 7) support that the agent correctly found and reported Developer = “Tiburon” and Release date = “8/13/2026”, but the publisher value is not visible in the provided evidence and the agent therefore could not report it. While the agent was appropriately non-fabricating and respected constraints (no sign-in, no purchase/download), the task is an information-retrieval task with a correctness/completeness bar: the user needed all three fields. Additionally, the evidence does not confirm the game was actually selected from a “Best sellers” section (the product page is open, but the best-sellers list itself is not evidenced), which further weakens task completion, though the more important failure is the missing publisher deliverable.\n\nOutcome: The agent partially completed the request (developer + release date) but failed to deliver the full required set (publisher/developer/release date) from the product page, so an average user would not consider the task completed.",
